{
"from": 116,
"to": 121,
"text": "No boot path is touched (test modules move and private functions are extracted), so there is no smoke entry and no live leg. The local pre-push gate is entry 1. The touched stand checks run in `stand-repeat` and the `a11y` leg. Moving a unit-test module out of line moves its crate's coverage reading with no code changed (testing rule, Not yet measured; history amd-h4ip3qlm), so the coverage leg reads the floors. Step 2 moves the public `Key`'s doc comment, with its `[`KEY_NAMES`]` intra-doc link, into a new file, so the doc leg is listed (tests · decision/doc-leg-gates-public-doc-edits)."
},
{
"from": 123,
"to": 131,
"text": "Entries 6–9 call the chunk's own instruments under `.andromeda/cache/chunks/2026-11-20-codebase-health/evidence/`, written at P4: - `bars.py` — the audit's recipe over every tracked or untracked `.rs` file, the class line `upstream/main`. Its PASS   is no file of ours over 800 but the seven targets left, and no function of ours over 15. It reads `bars: FAIL` at   the base: ours over 800 outside the seven, 3; ours over 15, 7 (`bars-base.txt`). - `test_paths.py` — the workspace's `cargo test -- --list` against `test-paths-base.txt`, recorded on the untouched   tree. - `scope_guard.py` — what changed since the base stays inside the twelve files and touches no upstream-authored one.   It reads PASS at the base."
},
{
"from": 133,
"to": 137,
"text": "Each instrument's known-verdict controls ran at P5, before its first graded use. The readings are in the run dir's `p5-controls.md`. `bars.py`'s FAIL side is the base reading, and its PASS side was read on a scratch clone holding the subject trimmed. `scope_guard.py` read both sides on a scratch clone (an allowed edit PASS; an upstream-authored edit and an outside file FAIL). `test_paths.py` read its FAIL side against a base list with one path removed and one added, an input operand alone. The census entry read 12 on a scratch clone with one `println!` added."
},
{
"from": 139,
"to": 140,
"text": "The founder criterion has no listed producer: phase P4 writes `founder-forks.md` into its own run dir, a step outside the block. The review card names it, and the wrap reads it."
},
{
